  "reason": "The records collectively disclose the essential processing concept and strengthening rationale. R1, R3, R5, R6, R9, R11, R15, R18, and R20 describe mechanically alloyed or milled HEA powders followed by vacuum SPS, while R2 and R4 show that high-energy milling under argon converts elemental mixtures into solid solutions through severe deformation. R15 directly connects longer milling, refinement, and Hall-Petch hardening after SPS; R8 independently establishes nanocrystalline grain-boundary strengthening; and R19, in the closely related CoCrFeMnNi system, attributes strength to fine grains and accumulated dislocations. Other records establish solid-solution/lattice-distortion strengthening and rapid SPS densification. None supplies the exact CoCrFeNiTi composition, short 1–6 h milling schedule, 900–1000 °C SPS window, or the specific 83% FCC/17% BCC balance, but these are alloy-specific selections and optimization rather than a new processing concept. An expert could plausibly combine the records to propose HEBM followed by short vacuum SPS and predict grain-boundary, dislocation, and solid-solution strengthening."
